  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "An angle $\\theta $ in the coordinate plane (measured in the usual way) has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={63}^{∘}.$ List, in ascending order, all the possible values of $\\theta $ in the range ${0}^{∘}\\le \\theta <{360}^{∘}.$\n\nIn ascending order, $\\theta $ can be equal to ${63}^{∘},$\n{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘},\\,\\,{243}^{∘},$ and\n{{field-2}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's remind ourselves of the relationship between ${\\theta }_{R}$ and $\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225277/assets/708bfa7367283d4be71b5df2c426862041b0a5ca939550e74f20e0e642856045.png)\n\nUsing ${\\theta }_{R}={63}^{∘},$ let's calculate all possible values of $\\theta .$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the first quadrant, then $\\theta ={\\theta }_{R}={63}^{∘}.$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the second quadrant, then $\\theta ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R}={180}^{∘}-{63}^{∘}={117}^{∘}.$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the third quadrant, then $\\theta ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R}={180}^{∘}+{63}^{∘}={243}^{∘}.$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the fourth quadrant, then $\\theta ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R}={360}^{∘}-{63}^{∘}={297}^{∘}.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, $\\theta $ can be equal to ${63}^{∘},$ ${117}^{∘},$ ${243}^{∘},$ and ${297}^{∘}.$",
